**Reasoning**:
- The regression (0.0240 in only 22s) indicates the optimizer terminated far too early — the greedy search hadn't annealed to a local optimum. Raising rounds to 300 with slower decay (0.95) lets each seed converge properly.
- History shows cycling kick magnitudes (0.006/0.015/0.04) with repeated re-optimization is the single most effective mechanism for escaping local optima — Attempt 1 (0.9673) used exactly this. The current version's fixed 0.02 kick with only 4 restarts is insufficient.
- A long final polish at s0=0.004 with 800 candidates squeezes out the last few percent of min-area.
- Budget of 300s stays safely under the 360s limit while using nearly all available time — the metric weights min_area far more than eval_time, so trading time for quality is correct (all high-scoring attempts took 290–320s).
